/; Assignment sits at precedence 1 in OperatorPrecedence::getInfixPrecedence,
/; which admits it in expression position. An assignment used as a value yields
/; its (first) target after the store, so `x = y = 3` binds right-to-left.
/; See docs/known-issues/assignment-in-expression-position.md
var y: int = 0
var x: int = 0
x = y = 3
print(x, "\n")
print(y, "\n")
